  "fitting": {
    "_source": {
      "std": "ASME B16.11", "edition": "2016", "table": "Table 1",
      "title": "Socket-Welding Elbows, Tees, and Crosses",
      "printedUnit": "mm", "read": "2026-10-10",
      "note": [
        "A socket-welding 90 degree elbow is a COMPACT FORGED BLOCK, not a sweeping",
        "curve. The dimension that locates it is centre-to-bottom-of-socket, A --",
        "how far from the fitting's centre the pipe end lands. There is no long",
        "radius at this size.",
        "Tee and cross share the elbow's A at the same NPS and class."
      ]
    },
